{"reasoning":"We face an orienteering problem with time windows and want a quick heuristic that runs under time. We adopt a simple greedy tour builder: for each possible site as the starting point, we “start” at the site’s opening time (no travel cost to first site), then repeatedly pick the next unvisited site that yields the best value per (travel+visit time) while still fitting its time window. We account for waiting if we arrive before a site’s open time, and only select candidates whose entire visit (including any wait) finishes before the site’s closing time. We run this greedy procedure once from each possible starting site and keep the sequence that yields the highest total value. This runs in O(N^3) in the worst case, which is efficient for typical tour sizes and respects the 5-minute limit.","code":"from pydantic import BaseModel
from typing import Dict, List, Any
from system.message import Info, BaseMessageDataType
from model.strategy_type import StrategyType
from model.base import BaseStrategy

class OptimalTouringCustomStrategy:
    def __init__(self, model: BaseStrategy):
        self._model = model
        self.name = self._model.name
        self.history = self._model.history
        self.strategy_type = StrategyType.Custom

    def update_model_field(self, field_name: str, value: Any):
        if hasattr(self._model, field_name):
            setattr(self._model, field_name, value)

    def receive_message(self, message: Info) -> Info:
        sites_data: Dict[int, Dict[str, int]] = message.message[0].data[0]

        # Convert site windows to minutes and precompute coordinates
        sites = {}
        for sid, info in sites_data.items():
            sites[sid] = {
                'x': info['avenue'],
                'y': info['street'],
                'visit': info['desiredtime'],
                'value': info['value'],
                'open': info['beginhour'] * 60,
                'close': info['endhour'] * 60
            }

        def manhattan(a, b):
            return abs(a['x'] - b['x']) + abs(a['y'] - b['y'])

        best_value = 0
        best_path: List[int] = []
        all_ids = list(sites.keys())
        n = len(all_ids)

        # Try greedy starting from each site
        for start in all_ids:
            visited = [start]
            t = sites[start]['open']  # we start at its opening
            # finish first visit
            t = max(t, sites[start]['open']) + sites[start]['visit']
            total_value = sites[start]['value']
            remaining = set(all_ids) - {start}
            # greedy fill
            while True:
                best_ratio = -1.0
                best_next = None
                best_arrival = 0
                for nxt in remaining:
                    travel = manhattan(sites[visited[-1]], sites[nxt])
                    arrive = t + travel
                    # if early, wait
                    if arrive < sites[nxt]['open']:
                        arrive = sites[nxt]['open']
                    finish = arrive + sites[nxt]['visit']
                    if finish <= sites[nxt]['close']:
                        ratio = sites[nxt]['value'] / (travel + sites[nxt]['visit'])
                        if ratio > best_ratio:
                            best_ratio = ratio
                            best_next = nxt
                            best_arrival = finish
                if best_next is None:
                    break
                # commit
                visited.append(best_next)
                t = best_arrival
                total_value += sites[best_next]['value']
                remaining.remove(best_next)

            if total_value > best_value:
                best_value = total_value
                best_path = visited

        visited_sites = best_path
        return Info(
            sender=self.__class__.__name__,
            receiver=message.sender,
            difficulty=message.difficulty,
            message=[BaseMessageDataType(data=visited_sites, type='custom')]
        )"}
